%% 06-flow-readings-history.mmd - Request/response flow: readings history (four parents), paginated, filtered, sorted, conditional
%% Basis: BRIEF §5, §6 (analytical view: pagination, filtering by jurisdiction and time window, sorting, conditional GET); WP §4.6, §5.6, §5.7, §10.2-10.4
%% Decisions: my-decisions §10, §11. OQ-04 DECIDED (YOU): jurisdiction = path parent, everything else = query. Sort syntax DECIDED (OQ-23).
%% PROPOSALS: defaults and caps, tie-break by installation_id, scope rule for province / district / substation.
%% OPEN: how the ETag is built (OQ-29, Phase 6).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as User
  participant M as Middleware
  participant S as Service
  participant DB as MongoDB
  U->>M: GET readings under ONE parent, with from, to, sort, offset, limit
  Note over U,M: parent = /installations/{id}, /substations/{id}, /districts/{id} or /provinces/{id}, then /readings
  M->>M: authenticate (diagram 04b)
  M->>DB: load the path parent
  alt parent does not exist
    M-->>U: 404
  else parent exists
    M->>M: parent inside caller jurisdiction? (a province route is broader than a district user)
    alt outside jurisdiction
      M-->>U: 403
    else inside
      alt from, to, sort, offset or limit invalid
        M-->>U: 400 + error[] per field
      else valid
        M->>S: query readings under this parent
        S->>DB: installation ids under the parent (derived ids on installations, or the one installation)
        S->>DB: readings for those ids inside the time window
        DB-->>S: matching set
        S->>S: count total, sort by requested field then installation_id, slice by offset and limit
        S-->>M: count, data, next and previous links
        M->>M: compute ETag and Last-Modified
        alt If-None-Match (or If-Modified-Since) still current
          M-->>U: 304 Not Modified, empty body
        else changed or no validator sent
          M-->>U: 200 + ETag + Last-Modified + {count, next, previous, data}
        end
      end
    end
  end
  Note over U,DB: Only GET exists on the substation, district and province readings. POST readings is only under an installation (diagram 05)
